# Copy to .env and fill in real values before running run_example.py.
# Gitignored -- same bare `.env` rule as every other example in this
# directory.
#
# This example uses FoundryChatClient + AzureCliCredential -- the SAME
# client/credential Microsoft's own upstream sample uses, not a
# simplified stand-in. That means AUTHENTICATION is NOT an env var: run
#     az login
# once in your shell before running this script. AzureCliCredential reads
# your Azure CLI's own local token cache, not anything in this file.
#
# FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT/FOUNDRY_MODEL below are read directly by
# FoundryChatClient itself (confirmed from its own __init__ docstring),
# not passed explicitly in run_example.py -- same as upstream's own
# FoundryChatClient(credential=credential) call, which also takes no
# project_endpoint argument.

# Your Azure AI Foundry PROJECT endpoint (Foundry portal -> your project
# -> Overview -- a project endpoint, e.g.
# https://my-project.services.ai.azure.com, NOT the same resource type as
# examples/maf_webapp's/maf_cli's AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT).
FOUNDRY_PROJECT_ENDPOINT=https://parapetai-foundry-resource1.services.ai.azure.com

# The model deployment name inside that project.
#FOUNDRY_MODEL=gpt-4o
FOUNDRY_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# Optional -- governs this script by a real control-plane-provisioned
# agent's bundle instead of the policy set bundled with parapetai-agent
# (base permits -- see run_example.py's own module docstring). Get all
# three from the control plane's agent detail page ("Integrating this
# agent") after provisioning an agent there. THIS example's own agent,
# not a different maf_sample_0N/'s. Leave unset to run against the
# bundled default -- the Cedar principal itself then falls back to
# Agent::"anonymous" too (still evaluated by default-deny, never a
# bypass; set PARAPETAI_AGENT_ID for a real name once you have one). The
# pulled bundle stays in memory only (never written to disk) -- see
# run_example.py for why.
# PARAPETAI_AGENT_ID=pa-xxxxxxxxxxxx
# PARAPETAI_AGENT_SECRET=<printed once on the agent detail page after provisioning>
# PARAPETAI_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=http://localhost:8090
